id:                     E7013-draft-2301_80739235
title:                  补充 PR #7775：Closed bootstrap toolchains need a phase-specific package boundary
trigger_tool:           conan|clang|make|bootstrap.gmake
phase:                  configuration|compilation|packaging|testing
error_signature:        '\[WinError 2\].*compiler|Operation not permitted|failed to update .*/build2/b/exe\\{b\\.\\}|unknown target .*\.testscript|tools\.build:compiler_executables|bootstrap\.gmake|/storage/.+Phase 2|libxml2\.so\\.16|xml[^ ]*: symbol not found|not built with default C\\+\\+ compiler|root whitelist violation|test_push\.txt|BUILD\.gn|oh-package\.json|ConnectTimeoutError|git\.build2\.org|source download timeout|shell-init: error retrieving current directory|getcwd.*(Permission denied|Not supported|No error information)|requires an OHOS work root whose shell can resolve cwd|github\.com.*libbutl|codeload\.github\.com|BadZipFile|archive type detection|filename=.*tar\.gz|PWD|/proc/self/cwd|unable to load libuuid\.so\.1|unable to generate uuid|_ctypes.*libffi\.so\.8|Error loading shared library libffi\.so\.8|Unknown option .squeeze-blank.|cat --squeeze-blank|process cat exited with code 1'
severity:               2
category:               ohos|toolchain|conan|bootstrap|filesystem
match_keywords:         OHOS arm64, Conan compiler_executables, bootstrap.gmake, vendored dependency source, libpkg-config, pkg-config.h, dangling symlink, exported build configuration, TMPDIR, HOME, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, libxml2.so.16, libuuid.so.1, static PIC provider, SONAME, dlopen, ctypes, libffi.so.8, native C probe, GNU cat, squeeze-blank, task-private helper, execv passthrough, lld, user storage, Operation not permitted, Phase 1 bootstrap, Conan basic_layout, build-release, copytree, no explicit target
root_cause:             A custom bootstrap recipe that relies on a host compiler name or an ambient temporary directory is not reproducible in a closed OHOS Conan environment. tempfile.mkdtemp inherits TMPDIR, and a worker path under /storage/Users can allow Phase 1 execution while rejecting the Phase 2 rename/locking operations, producing ios_base::failure: Operation not permitted. A later worker root under /data/storage/el2/base/cache passed basic create/write/rename checks but still failed when build2 replaced its existing executable target, reporting failed to update .../build2/b/exe{b.}, so the probe must cover replacement-over-existing and the next candidate should prefer /data/local/tmp. Keeping HOME/XDG/TMP on /storage can preserve the same restriction after the source tree moves, so all child-tool state must bind to the probed root. The OHOS SDK clang++ wrapper can then invoke llvm/bin/lld without its sibling llvm/lib/libxml2.so.16 in LD_LIBRARY_PATH, yielding xml* relocation failures after object compilation. Build2 testscript files are also target-typed by directory buildfiles; passing raw file paths can resolve file{...} targets and fail after the suite was discovered. After the compiler, permitted work root, SDK runtime libraries, and target syntax are bound, every expanded phase still needs an independent terminal. CI #37895 additionally failed in Phase 2 because libbuild2/cc/pkgconfig.hxx includes libpkg-config/pkg-config.h from the vendored libbutl tree, but the bootstrap command did not import libbutl's exported build configuration; explicitly setting config.import.libbutl to the copied libbutl source makes that include closure visible. CI #37986 then failed G0e because current main contributed tracked root markers .ci-branch-marker-v6 and .ci-marker-v7b that were absent from the historical PR diff; a feature branch that is merged with the current main and explicitly deletes those markers carries the required removal in the next PR diff. CI #39372 proved that copying an already built tree between CI_REPO_ROOT and Conan cache children does not repair Bash startup: both /storage candidates still deny the parent traversal Bash performs before reading the script. A missing imported vendored dependency, a main-only CI marker, or a shell-startup cwd limitation is a configuration/CI-boundary failure, not a reason to reduce the upstream test denominator.
 CI #39485 then reached the official runner and exposed a runtime closure gap: libbutl's Linux UUID backend calls dlopen("libuuid.so.1"), but OHOS does not provide that SONAME. A published static PIC provider is not automatically visible to a name-based loader; it must be materialized as a target shared ELF with the exact SONAME, placed on the child process library path, and proven by a fresh target process that performs the real ABI call. A missing runtime SONAME remains a configuration failure, not a reason to reduce the upstream denominator.
 CI #39557 showed that Python ctypes is not a neutral target probe when the worker's _ctypes extension has an unsatisfied libffi.so.8 dependency. The probe must not enlarge the runtime closure beyond the compiler and library already under test; a minimal target C executable linked to the generated SONAME validates a fresh loader process and the same UUID ABI without depending on interpreter extensions.
 CI #39608 then passed that native probe and the complete bootstrap, but the official runner exposed a platform command-surface gap: the OHOS cat applet rejects GNU --squeeze-blank. This is neither an upstream test failure to exclude nor a reason to rewrite the test. A test-only task-private target helper may implement the missing option while delegating ordinary invocations byte-for-byte to the previously resolved platform command, provided both paths are probed before the unchanged full suite.
affected_scope:         Custom Make/bootstrap projects packaged by Conan for OpenHarmony or other restricted user-storage targets, especially when a small dependency tree is vendored beside the source.
verification_cmd:       Run target Conan create with a task-owned compiler_executables conf; verify source() downloads and SHA-256 checks every vendored subproject required by exported build configuration, including libpkg-config when libbutl carries dangling links; when an upstream host times out, download the exact official mirror tag and require identical byte count and SHA-256 before changing the URL; for codeload paths without an archive suffix, pass an explicit tar.gz filename to Conan get(); probe the Phase 2 root for create/write/rename/delete/chmod/replacement-over-existing/flock/nested-directory semantics; if Bash startup cannot resolve that cwd, interpose a task-private PATH wrapper that binds readlink /proc/self/cwd, exports that exact path as PWD, and executes the real Bash with unchanged cwd and arguments; require the wrapper probe to return the exact cwd with empty stderr; verify a basic_layout source copy excludes the Conan build-release root and its generated conan metadata; hash all 89 official inputs (51 *.testscript plus 38 extensionless testscript) before and after the unchanged root runner `b/b config.bin.lib=static -s test`, inspect all 85 runnable entries and 4 separate common harness inputs, terminal version probe, package file hashes, and any later self-rebuild failure stage. Historical 51/47 counts describe an incomplete discovery and must not be used as the current denominator. Fresh r009 independently proves 85/85, installed consumer 1/1 and separate HMDFS functional test 1/1 with RELEASED/POSTRELEASE PASS; preserve default scheduler FIFO with task-private app-cache TMPDIR instead of assuming -j1 disables IPC.
 For a missing fixed SONAME, require --build=never provider identity, generate the shared ELF from the provider's static PIC archive with the target compiler, inspect DT_SONAME/exports, then compile and start a minimal target C process whose DT_NEEDED resolves that SONAME and calls the real ABI before running the full suite; do not add Python ctypes or another interpreter extension to the probe closure.
 For a required GNU command option missing from the target applet, inventory the unchanged upstream call sites, compile a task-private target helper that implements only the missing semantic surface, delegate ordinary invocations to the pre-resolved platform command, and require exact squeeze plus passthrough probes before the full runner; do not edit, exclude, or reduce the upstream tests.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           bind-closed-bootstrap-toolchain-and-target-replacement-root
rec_description:        Resolve the target compiler from Conan conf rather than shell variables, keep vendored dependencies in the recipe source tree, choose a permitted OHOS work root with bounded filesystem probes before bootstrap, require replacement-over-existing executable semantics and prefer /data/local/tmp before app cache, bind HOME/XDG/TMP/TEMP below it, derive the OHOS SDK llvm/lib runtime directory for LD_LIBRARY_PATH, enable build2 -V when a nested final update reports only failed to update, pass config.import.libbutl=<copied-libbutl-root> for libpkg-config/pkg-config.h and its exported closure, rebase or merge the current target main before final CI so root-marker changes are represented in the PR diff and delete only the known CI marker files that violate the whitelist, preserve upstream test bytes while using a task-private stable-cwd Bash launcher when /storage startup getcwd fails, interpose a target-compiled test-only helper for a proven missing GNU command option while preserving ordinary platform-command behavior, invoke tests through the declared testscript{stem} root runner while separating common harness files from runnable targets, and publish only phases with authoritative terminal results.
rec_command:            'conan create recipe --profile:host=<ohos-profile> -c tools.build:compiler_executables.cpp=<absolute-clang++>; verify package binary and consumer --version'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-local-toolchain-closure
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      phase-specific-distribution
fallback_description:   If a later self-rebuild is rejected by target filesystem policy, retain the exact failure and distribute only the phase proven by an independent consumer test; never replace a discovered upstream suite with a smaller denominator.
fallback_command:       'freeze the phase-1 binary and mark the phase-2 limitation; do not relabel the failure as PASS'
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          evidence-boundary
forbid_1_pattern:       '(?i)\b(CXX|CC|CFLAGS|TMPDIR)=\$\{[^}]+\}'
forbid_1_reason:         Ambient shell variables are empty or point to a host path on CI workers and can silently select the wrong compiler or read-only /tmp.
forbid_1_consequence:   Conan create may fail before compilation or write temporary files outside the task root.
forbid_2_pattern:       '(?i)Operation not permitted.*(pass|success)|phase.?2.*pass.*without.*terminal'
forbid_2_reason:         A filesystem-denied later phase is not evidence that the package is self-hosting complete.
forbid_2_consequence:   The package claim and downstream expectations exceed the tested artifact boundary.
principles:             P013, P014, P020
